  "id": "COMPOUND:24290 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (S)-2-Methylbutanoate may interact with A2780cisR through multiple pathways. The first pathway involves the protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is targeted by [(2H-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)methyl](prop-2-en-1-yl)amine, a compound that has a target relationship with A2780cisR. The second pathway links (S)-2-Methylbutanoate to FaDu, which is targeted by Calenduloside C, also targeting A2780cisR. These findings indicate that (S)-2-Methylbutanoate may act as a modulator of signaling pathways involving phosphatases and other targets that ultimately influence A2780cisR. The evidence is consistent with a potential role of (S)-2-Methylbutanoate in regulating cellular processes through these molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
